' The last king, Tarquinius Superbus, was expelled in 509 BC, and the Republic was established. The Roman Republic was a period of significant political and social development, marked by the struggle between the patricians and the plebeians. The patricians, the wealthy and powerful families, initially held most of the political power, while the plebeians, the common people, fought for greater rights and representation. One of the key figures in this struggle was Gaius Marcius Coriolanus, a Roman general who was known for his military prowess and his opposition to the plebeians. Coriol\n'
